.TH KAGI-TLS-CERT 1 "November 2026" "Kagi 0.39.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kagi-tls-cert \- generate a self-signed ML-DSA-87 HTTPS identity
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bash scripts/kagi-tls-cert
.RI [ OUTPUT-DIRECTORY ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writes
.I server-key.pem
and
.I server-cert.pem
in the specified directory.
The default directory is
.IR /etc/kagi/tls .
The script replaces files with those names if they exist.
.PP
The installed OpenSSL must advertise ML-DSA-87 signature support.
The generated certificate is self-signed.
Configure explicit trust in peers and clients that support ML-DSA X.509.
Keep the private key readable only by the user that needs it.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KAGI_TLS_NAME
Certificate common name.
The default is
.BR kagi.local .
.TP
.B KAGI_TLS_DAYS
Certificate validity in days.
The default is 825.
.TP
.B KAGI_TLS_SAN
OpenSSL subjectAltName value.
The default is the certificate name with a
.B DNS:
prefix.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kagi-cluster-host (1),
.BR kagi-install (1),
.BR openssl-req (1)
